Subject: [PATCH] logging: structure non-GUI notifications without changing
 secure output policy

Scripted diff: /private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/node-ui-notifications.json --apply --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/ui-conversion-receipt.json

Formatting: git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style "{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}" HEAD -- src/noui.cpp src/noui.h src/test/logging_event_tests.cpp

Convert all7 direct non-GUI notification producers. Keep original Error/Warning/Info selection, SECURE guard before capture, literal prefix punctuation, untranslated content, stderr output and false returns. MessageText is existing opaque prose, not claimed structured inner fields. Redirect hooks preserve test infrastructure behavior; init events share a schema. Support adjustments append MessageText/Caption and update the redirect API comment.

Manual native controls exercise actual ordinary UI methods at all3 levels and secure no-file-log behavior while comparing original stderr/return values; init prose includes percent and newline bytes. AST/event lint386 and diff checks pass. Native execution pending next combined source gate, not inherited from171.

